SUMMARY:EXHIBITION – FORUM ON SUPPORTING INDUSTRY AND THE SUPPLY-DEMAND 
 CONNECTION CONFERENCE FOR THE SUPPLY CHAIN 2025
LOCATION:WTC EXPO International Exhibition Center - Hall A\, A19 Hung Vuon
 g Street\, Binh Duong Ward\, Ho Chi Minh City\, Vietnam
DESCRIPTION:Dates: 2025-12-04 to 2025-12-05\nHours: 09:00 - 17:00\nVenue: 
 WTC EXPO International Exhibition Center\nHall: Hall A\nAddress: A19 Hung
  Vuong Street\, Binh Duong Ward\, Ho Chi Minh City\, Vietnam\nEvent page:
  https://wtcbinhduong.vn/en/su-kien/exhibition-forum-on-supporting-indust
 ry-and-the-supply-demand-connection-cofference-for-the-supply-chain-2025/
 \nWebsite: https://www.intelligentcommunity.org/icf_global_summit_2025\nS
 tatus: Confirmed\nVietnamese name: TRIỂN LÃM – DIỄN ĐÀN VỀ CÔ
 NG NGHIỆP HỖ TRỢ VÀ HỘI NGHỊ KẾT NỐI CUNG CẦU CHUỖI CU
 NG ỨNG 2025\n\nGENERAL INFORMATION\n\n- Time: 09:00 – 17:00 | Decembe
 r 4–5\, 2025.\n- Venue: Hall A – WTC EXPO A19\, Hung Vuong Street\, B
 inh Duong Ward\, Ho Chi Minh City.\n- Concurrent event: ICF Global Summit
  2025 – For Smart City Binh Duong\, taking place from December 2–3\, 
 2025.\n\nAs Vietnam’s industrial sector shifts toward a greener\, smart
 er\, and more sustainable direction\, the Ho Chi Minh City Supporting Ind
 ustry Association (HASI)\, in collaboration with Becamex Group\, WTC Binh
  Duong\, HEPZA\, ITPC\, and Thaco Industries\, is organizing the largest 
 annual event of the Supporting Industry sector.\n\nUnder the theme “Con
 necting Value Chains – Advancing Sustainable Industrial Development\,
 ” the program brings together:\n\n- Over 200 enterprises and 60 industr
 ial parks nationwide.\n- More than 3\,000 industry professionals and visi
 tors.\n- A comprehensive series of Exhibitions – Conferences – B2B Ma
 tchmaking activities within the same venue.\n\nBooth registration link: h
 ttps://forms.gle/m4NVnLJGSLR9wvHs9\n\nWHY YOU SHOULD VISIT THE EXHIBITION
 ?\n\n- The exhibition takes place alongside the Supporting Industry Forum
 \, CEO Summit\, and the Supply–Demand Connection Conference\, bringing 
 together hundreds of domestic and international enterprises.\n- The event
  is part of the Global Summit – Intelligent Community Forum 2025\, expe
 cted to welcome more than 500 international delegates.\n- The supply–de
 mand matching program involves major FDI enterprises\, industry associati
 ons\, and industrial park authorities.\n- Multiple in-depth conferences w
 ith the presence of leading experts and industry leaders.\n- The Gala Din
 ner gathers over 300 distinguished guests\, creating opportunities for ne
 tworking\, business exchange\, and expanding partnerships after the event
 .
